# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scraped third-party match data — NEVER commit.
#
# Everything here is regenerable by running the scrapers, is large (~30MB),
# and is Opta/Pulse data that must not be redistributed. Two layers:
#   1. the directories every scraper actually writes to (primary), and
#   2. filename/extension backstops, so a stray data file dropped at the repo
#      root — or a scraper whose output path changes — still cannot be
#      committed by accident.
# The repo tracks only source (.py/.html/.md), so these backstops hide nothing
# legitimate. If you ever add a real root-level config.json or data.csv, add
# it deliberately with: git add -f <file>
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments — a '#' only starts a comment at the
# start of a line. Keep every pattern on its own line.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. scraper output directories
cache/
Newcache/

# 2. backstops for scraped data landing elsewhere.
# All JSON/CSV in this repo is state or scraped data — source is only
# .py/.html/.md. Blanket-ignored so no data file can be committed by accident,
# anywhere in the tree. To track a genuine config file: git add -f <file>
*.json
*.csv
# write-then-rename temp files (e.g. deductions.json.tmp, cache/*.json.tmp)
*.tmp
*.json.tmp

# Local app state — rebuilt on first run; changes on every result entered.
# (root JSON is also covered above; kept explicit for clarity)
data.json
deductions.json

# Runtime / process / logs
.server.pid
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editors / OS
.claude/
.zed/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
